g": "TI-201", "type": "analog", "high_limit": null, "low_limit": 10.0, "deadband": 0.0, "priority": "high", "enabled": true}}, "removed": []}, "latency_ms": 0.020000035874545574, "intended_entities": ["alarms.alarm_TI201_LL"], "referenced_entities": ["points.TI-201"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:5c36a73b4c1d2de1572720df5fcdfadf57212e64b3121822dbe294c91f962227", "final_hash": "sha256:c2c6f084ec267c5d8f6b86c605eff94c847bd464cdc720e9489a9404a9fef9ca", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 45512, "output_tokens": 380, "latency_ms": 11781.239200034179, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我将为 TI-201 创建两个独立的模拟量报警：HH 报警（高高限 100）和 LL 报警（低低限 10），优先级都设为 high。", "reasoning": "The user wants to create alarms for a point tag \"TI-201\":\n1. A high-high (HH) alarm at 100 with high priority\n2. A low-low (LL) alarm at 10 with high priority\n\nI need to use `create_analog_alarm` to create these alarms. However, the create_analog_alarm function has parameters for `high_limit` and `low_limit` on a single alarm definition. \n\nLooking at the function, it seems like one alarm can have both a high_limit and a low_limit. But the user wants separate HH and LL alarms. Let me think about this...\n\nActually, in typical SCADA systems, HH and LL are separate alarm points. So I should create two separate analog alarms:\n1. One for the HH limit at 100\n2. One for the LL limit at 10\n\nLet me create two alarms with distinct IDs like `alarm_TI201_HH` and `alarm_TI201_LL`."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 45962, "output_tokens": 155, "latency_ms": 6581.257599988021, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "已成功为 **TI-201** 创建两个报警：\n\n| 报警 ID | 类型 | 限值 | 优先级 |\n|---------|------|------|--------|\n| `alarm_TI201_HH` | 高高限 (HH) | **100** | high |\n| `alarm_TI201_LL` | 低低限 (LL) | **10** | high |\n\n当 TI-201 的值超过 100 或低于 10 时，将触发对应的高优先级报警。如需调整限值或增加死区（deadband），请告知。", "reasoning": "Both alarms were created successfully. Let me summarize the results for the user."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 91474, "output_tokens": 535, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 18600.153299979866}, "judge": null}
