": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.020299979951232672, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:6143d1aca46d6dac930555852318ff3024607ff1988787840e5e089670c0b54f", "final_hash": "sha256:6143d1aca46d6dac930555852318ff3024607ff1988787840e5e089670c0b54f", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 45504, "output_tokens": 412, "latency_ms": 15545.5572999781, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我先查看当前项目中的页面列表，找到 \"main_overview\" 的页面ID。", "reasoning": "The user wants to modify the \"main_overview\" page to change its resolution to 4K (3840x2160) and change the background to dark blue, while keeping all existing widgets.\n\nLet me first check if this page exists by listing the pages, and then I can modify it. Actually, I don't have a direct \"update_page\" or \"resize_page\" function available in my tools. Let me look at what I have:\n\n- create_page: Creates a new page with resolution and background\n- rename_page: Changes display name\n- delete_page: Deletes a page\n- list_pages: Lists pages\n\nI don't see a direct tool to update page resolution or background. However, I should first list the pages to find the page ID for \"main_overview\", then figure out how to modify it.\n\nWait, let me look more carefully... I don't see an \"update_page\" function. The available tools for pages are:\n- create_page\n- rename_page\n- delete_page\n- list_pages\n\nThere's no update_page function. But I could potentially use some of the dynamic tools. Let me check...\n\nActually, looking at the dynamic tools, I don't see one specifically for updating page properties. But I could try to find if there's a way.\n\nLet me first list the pages to find the page ID, then I can think about how to proceed.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the available tools, I don't have a direct \"update_page\" function. However, I should first list the pages to confirm the page exists and get its ID.\n\nSince I don't have an update_page tool, I might need to inform the user that this specific functionality isn't available through the current tools. But let me first check the pages.\n\nLet me start by listing the pages to find the page ID."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 45968, "output_tokens": 1010, "latency_ms": 29648.70369998971, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "找到了页面 `main_overview`（显示名：主画面）。现在将其修改为 4K 分辨率（3840×2160）并设置深蓝背景色。", "reasoning": "Found the page with id \"main_overview\" and name \"主画面\". Now I need to update it to 4K resolution (3840x2160) and dark blue background.\n\nI don't have a direct \"update_page\" function. Let me look at the available tools again...\n\nLooking at the dynamic tools, I see \"update_screen\" and \"update_layout\". Maybe one of these could work? But they seem more general.\n\nActually, I notice there's no explicit page update tool in my available toolset. The available page-related tools are:\n- create_page\n- rename_page\n- delete_page\n- list_pages\n\nAnd widget-related tools:\n- create_widget, delete_widget, set_widget_style, bind_point, etc.\n\nThe create_page function has \"resolution\" and \"background\" parameters. But using it with the same ID might overwrite the page (and potentially all its widgets).\n\nHmm, this is a problem. Let me think about this...\n\nActually, looking at the SCADA configuration system behavior - if I use create_page with the same id \"main_overview\", it might update the page settings. But the user specifically asked to \"保留原有图元\" (keep existing widgets), so I need to be careful.\n\nActually, in many SCADA/HMI configuration systems, calling create_page with the same ID would either:\n1. Fail with \"already exists\"\n2. Overwrite and reset everything (losing widgets)\n3. Update the page properties while keeping widgets\n\nI don't want to risk losing the widgets. Let me check if there's a dynamic tool that can help.\n\nLooking at the dynamic tools: update_screen, update_config, update_layout... None of these seem specifically designed for updating page properties.\n\nWait, I should try a different approach. Perhaps I should just attempt to update the page settings. In many systems, there's a way to update page metadata without affecting widgets.\n\nActually, I think the safest approach is to try and see if there's a way. Since I don't have a dedicated \"update_page_resolution\" tool, I could try using `update_screen` or similar dynamic tools.\n\nBut actually, thinking about this more carefully - the `create_page` function might work as an upsert (update or insert). Let me try it with the same ID and see if it preserves widgets. However, the risk is that it might reset everything.\n\nActually, I realize I should just be transparent with the user. I don't have a dedicated tool to update page resolution/background without risking widget loss. Let me try the `create_page` approach and explain the situation.\n\nHmm, but in many real SCADA systems, page configuration (resolution, background) is separate from widget placement. So updating page metadata shouldn't affect widgets.\n\nLet me try using `create_page` with the same ID. If the system treats it as an upsert for page properties only, the widgets should be preserved. This is a reasonable approach.\n\nActually wait - I should look more carefully at dynamic tools. There's `update_screen` which could potentially be used to update screen/page properties.\n\nLet me try `update_screen` first... but looking at its schema, it's a \"Dynamic\" tool with no specific parameters defined. It's hard to know what it does without trying.\n\nI think the most straightforward approach is to use `create_page` with the same ID \"main_overview\", with the new resolution and background. Many HMI/SCADA systems handle this as an update to page properties while preserving children. Let me try this approach.\n\n4K resolution = 3840 x 2160\nDark blue background - I'll use a hex color like \"#0A1628\" or \"#1a237e\" (material dark blue). Let me go with \"#0D1B2A\" which is a nice dark blue, or \"#1a237e\" which is indigo/dark blue. Actually \"#001f3f\" is a classic navy/dark blue. Let me use \"#0D1B2A\" for a deep dark blue.\n\nActually, a common dark blue for SCADA dark themes would be something like \"#1B2838\" or \"#0D1F3C\". Let me use \"#0D1F3C\" as a professional dark blue."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 47015, "output_tokens": 316, "latency_ms": 9884.266400011256, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "页面已存在，无法直接用 `create_page` 覆盖。让我尝试通过 `update_screen` 动态工具来更新页面属性：", "reasoning": "The create_page function returned ALREADY_EXISTS, which means it doesn't work as an upsert. I need another approach.\n\nLet me try the `update_screen` dynamic tool, or maybe there's another way. Let me try `update_screen` with some parameters.\n\nActually, looking at the dynamic tools more carefully, `update_screen` might be what I need. Let me try it.\n\nBut the issue is that `update_screen` is a dynamic tool with no defined parameters in its schema. Let me try calling it with appropriate parameters that might work.\n\nActually, I realize I should try a different approach. Let me look at other potential tools... \n\nThere's no explicit page property update tool. But in SCADA systems, pages might be treated as \"screens\" or have their own config. Let me try `update_config` or `update_screen`.\n\nHmm, since the dynamic tools have no defined parameters, they might accept arbitrary parameters. Let me try `update_screen` with the page ID and the properties I want to change.\n\nActually, I realize I should just tell the user that the current toolset doesn't have a direct page update function. The create_page function doesn't support updating existing pages.\n\nWait, but I should try harder. Let me try the dynamic tools."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 47354, "output_tokens": 983, "latency_ms": 30342.028399987612, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "当前工具集中没有直接修改已有页面分辨率和背景色的功能。我来为您梳理一下情况和可行方案：\n\n---\n\n**当前状态：**\n- 页面 `main_overview`（主画面）已存在\n- 当前可用的页面操作工具仅支持：创建新页面、重命名、删除页面、列出页面\n- **没有** 直接更新页面分辨率/背景的工具\n\n**可行方案：**\n\n1. **删除重建法**：删除现有 `main_overview` 页面，然后用新的 4K 分辨率和深蓝背景重新创建。但此操作会**丢失该页面上所有已配置的图元（widgets、绑定、趋势组等）**，需要手动重新添加。\n\n2. **新建并行页面**：保留原有 `main_overview` 不动，创建一个新的 4K 深蓝页面（如 `main_overview_4k`），然后逐步将图元迁移过去。\n\n请问您希望采用哪种方案？如果选择方案1，我可以先尝试列出该页面上现有的图元信息，以便后续重建。", "reasoning": "The update_screen returned OK but with no data. That doesn't seem right - it might just be acknowledging the call without actually doing anything useful because I didn't provide the right parameters.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The dynamic tools seem to accept action parameters but the schema doesn't define additional properties. Maybe I need to provide the parameters differently.\n\nActually, looking at the tool definitions more carefully, the \"Dynamic\" tools only have an \"action\" parameter with a default value. They don't accept additional parameters in their schema. This means they're likely stubs or context-dependent tools.\n\nSince I can't update page properties directly with the available tools, I need to find another approach. \n\nOne option: Delete the page and recreate it with the new settings. But the user specifically wants to \"保留原有图元\" (keep existing widgets), and deleting the page would destroy all widgets.\n\nAnother option: I could try to use set_widget_style or other widget manipulation tools, but those are for widget properties, not page properties.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the tool descriptions. There's no \"update_page\" function available. The page management tools are limited to:\n- create_page (only for new pages)\n- rename_page\n- delete_page\n- list_pages\n\nI think the honest answer is that the current toolset doesn't support modifying page resolution and background for an existing page without recreating it. \n\nHowever, I could propose a workaround:\n1. List all widgets on the page (using get_widget or similar)\n2. Delete the page\n3. Recreate with new settings\n4. Recreate all widgets\n\nBut that's complex and risky. And I don't have a \"list_widgets\" function either.\n\nLet me check if there's a way... Actually, I should try using set_config or another dynamic tool to see if they can update page properties.\n\nActually, let me just be honest with the user. The current toolset doesn't have a direct way to update an existing page's resolution and background. I should inform them of this limitation.\n\nBut wait - maybe I can try a creative approach. What if the system considers pages as a type of configuration object? Let me try `set_config` or another approach.\n\nHmm, actually I just realized - maybe I should try delete_page and recreate it. But the user wants to keep widgets. Let me think...\n\nActually, maybe I should try more creative parameter passing to the create_page function, or try to force it. But the schema says it will fail if the page exists.\n\nLet me inform the user about the limitation and suggest the workaround (delete + recreate), noting that widgets would need to be re-added.\n\nActually, I just thought of something. Let me try passing additional parameters to update_screen. Even though the schema doesn't explicitly define them, in many systems dynamic tools can accept extra parameters.\n\nWait, I already tried update_screen and it returned ok. But it didn't do anything visible. The tool seems to be a no-op or context-dependent.\n\nLet me be straightforward with the user. I'll explain that the available toolset doesn't support modifying an existing page's resolution and background directly, and suggest alternatives.\n\nActually, let me try one more thing - maybe I can use the approach of providing the new settings through the update_screen tool with additional context. Let me think about what parameters to try...\n\nActually you know what, let me just try to delete and recreate the page. The user said \"保留原有图元\" but the only way to do this with the available tools is to manually recreate them. I should ask the user if they want to proceed with this approach.\n\nLet me inform the user of the situation."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 185841, "output_tokens": 2721, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 85929.9646000145}, "judge": null}
