rm for PUMP_A_RUN - specifically a \"running feedback disappearance\" alarm with high priority.\n\nPUMP_A_RUN is likely a digital point (boolean) that indicates whether a pump is running. When the pump is running, the tag is true (1), and when it stops (feedback disappears), it becomes false (0).\n\nFor a \"运行反馈消失\" (running feedback disappearance) alarm, this means we want to alarm when the tag becomes FALSE (pump stops/loses feedback). \n\nHowever, looking at the `create_digital_alarm` function, it \"fires when a boolean tag becomes true.\" This is the opposite of what we need - we need an alarm when the tag becomes FALSE.\n\nLet me think about this:\n- PUMP_A_RUN = true means pump is running (normal)\n- PUMP_A_RUN = false means pump feedback lost (alarm condition)\n\nThe `create_digital_alarm` fires when the tag becomes true. So to alarm on feedback loss (tag becoming false), we might need to:\n1. Use an inverted approach, or\n2. There might be a way to configure it\n\nActually, looking at the tool description again: \"Create a digital alarm that fires when a boolean tag becomes true.\" - this is the standard behavior. For a \"disappearance\" alarm, we typically want to alarm when the signal goes from true to false.\n\nIn many SCADA systems, you can create an alarm that monitors for the \"false\" state by convention - but this tool seems to only support alarming when true.\n\nLet me reconsider - perhaps in this SCADA system, we can still create the alarm and configure it appropriately. Or perhaps the system handles this differently.\n\nActually, let me re-read the requirement. The user says \"运行反馈消失报警\" which means \"running feedback disappearance alarm\". This is a common SCADA requirement where:\n- When pump should be running (commanded on) but the running feedback signal disappears (becomes false), an alarm should trigger.\n\n\n- In many SCADA systems, a digital alarm configured on PUMP_A_RUN might be set up to trigger when the tag goes FALSE, or there might be an \"inversion\" option. Since the tool only says \"fires when a boolean tag becomes true\", I might need to create a negated point, or there could be a `priority` parameter that could help. The most practical approach would be to create the digital alarm on PUMP_A_RUN and see if there's a way to configure it for the false condition, or potentially create an inverted auxiliary point to monitor.\n\nThe `create_digital_alarm` tool fires when a tag becomes true, but I need an alarm for when it becomes false—a common SCADA requirement. I should attempt to create the alarm with the available tool first, and if it doesn't support false-state detection, I'll need to inform the user about this limitation and explore alternatives like creating an inverted point or checking if there's a hidden configuration option."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 46229, "output_tokens": 710, "latency_ms": 23270.858800038695, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "PUMP_A_RUN 确认为 **digital** 类型点位。\n\n不过，我需要向您说明一个重要限制：\n\n⚠️ **当前可用的 `create_digital_alarm` 工具设计为：当布尔标签变为 TRUE 时触发报警。**\n\n而您的需求是\"**运行反馈消失**\"报警——即当 PUMP_A_RUN 从 TRUE 变为 **FALSE**（反馈丢失）时触发报警。这与工具的默认行为相反。\n\n**建议的解决方案：**\n\n1. **创建一个反转点位** —— 创建一个 `PUMP_A_RUN_LOST` 数字点位，通过脚本逻辑将其设为 PUMP_A_RUN 的取反值（当 PUMP_A_RUN = false 时，PUMP_A_RUN_LOST = true），然后对该点位配置报警。\n\n2. **使用脚本型报警** —— 创建一个 `on_change` 类型的脚本，在 PUMP_A_RUN 变为 false 时执行报警动作。\n\n您希望我采用哪种方案？还是您有其他想法？\n\nnext_state: ASK_USER", "reasoning": "Good, PUMP_A_RUN exists and is a digital type point. Now I need to create a digital alarm.\n\nFor \"运行反馈消失\" (running feedback disappearance), I need to alarm when the tag becomes FALSE. The `create_digital_alarm` fires when tag becomes true. \n\nHowever, in SCADA practice, \"运行反馈消失\" typically means we want to know when the pump is NOT running when it should be. This could be interpreted as:\n1. Alarm when PUMP_A_RUN goes from true to false\n2. Or sometimes it's implemented by monitoring the inverse\n\nSince the tool only fires \"when a boolean tag becomes true\", I might need to consider if there's an inversion or if I should inform the user about this limitation.\n\nLet me try to create the alarm with a descriptive ID. If the system only supports alarming on true, I'll need to explain this to the user. In many real SCADA systems, you can configure the alarm condition (on-true or on-false), but this tool seems limited.\n\nActually, let me just try to create it. The tool might handle this internally, or I may need to explain the limitation. Let me create the alarm with a good ID like \"alarm_pump_a_run_lost\" and tag PUMP_A_RUN, priority high.\n\nBut wait - if the alarm fires when tag becomes true, that would mean the alarm fires when the pump IS running, which is the opposite of what we want.\n\nI think I need to be honest with the user that the available `create_digital_alarm` tool is designed to fire when a tag becomes TRUE, and for a \"feedback disappearance\" alarm (which should fire when the tag becomes FALSE), we would need either:\n1. An inverted version of the point\n2. A different alarm configuration option\n\nLet me inform the user about this limitation and suggest alternatives. Actually, let me first try to see if there's any way to configure this. Maybe the system has some underlying mechanism.\n\n\nThe create_digital_alarm function lacks an \"inversion\" parameter, so I can't directly configure it for false-state detection. I should explain this constraint to the user and propose workarounds—either creating a complementary digital point that inverts PUMP_A_RUN's logic, or checking if the system supports an alternative alarm mechanism designed for false-state conditions."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 46936, "output_tokens": 434, "latency_ms": 18790.42550001759, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，我将采用**脚本方案**来实现运行反馈消失报警。这样可以直接监测 PUMP_A_RUN 变为 false 的情况，并触发报警。\n\n让我创建一个 `on_change` 类型的脚本来实现这个功能：", "reasoning": "The user is asking me to continue with the task. I'm in the ASK_USER stage and need to make a decision. The user wants to configure an alarm for PUMP_A_RUN when feedback disappears (goes false).\n\nSince the `create_digital_alarm` only fires when a tag becomes true, I proposed two solutions:\n1. Create an inverted point and alarm on that\n2. Use a script-based approach\n\nLet me go ahead with the script-based approach since it's more direct and doesn't require creating extra points. I'll create an `on_change` script that monitors PUMP_A_RUN and triggers an alarm when it becomes false.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The user might prefer the simpler approach. Let me use the script approach:\n\n1. Create a script with trigger `on_change` bound to PUMP_A_RUN\n2. The script body would check if the value becomes false and generate an alarm event\n\nLet me proceed with creating the script. This is a reasonable approach that uses the available tools.\n\nLet me create the script:"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 47431, "output_tokens": 127, "latency_ms": 8069.41390002612, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "脚本已创建成功。现在让我启用该脚本，确保报警功能生效：", "reasoning": "The script has been created successfully. Now I should enable the script to make it active. Let me check if I need to enable it or if it's enabled by default.\n\nActually, looking at the create_script result, it just says \"ok\": true. I should probably enable the script to make sure it's active. Let me use enable_script."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 47624, "output_tokens": 266, "latency_ms": 11628.133399994113, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "配置已完成！以下是您需求的实现总结：\n\n---\n\n✅ **PUMP_A 运行反馈消失报警已配置完成**\n\n| 配置项 | 详情 |\n|--------|------|\n| **监控点位** | PUMP_A_RUN (digital) |\n| **脚本ID** | script_pump_a_run_lost |\n| **触发条件** | PUMP_A_RUN 值变化时执行 |\n| **报警逻辑** | 当 PUMP_A_RUN = false（反馈消失）时触发 |\n| **报警优先级** | high |\n| **报警消息** | \"PUMP_A 运行反馈消失\" |\n| **脚本状态** | ✅ 已启用 |\n\n---\n\n当 PUMP_A_RUN 从 true 变为 false（运行反馈丢失）时，系统将自动生成一条高优先级报警。\n\nnext_state: DONE", "reasoning": "The script has been created and enabled. Let me summarize what was done for the user.\n\nThe task is complete:\n1. Created an on_change script (script_pump_a_run_lost) bound to PUMP_A_RUN\n2. The script checks when PUMP_A_RUN becomes false and generates a high-priority alarm\n3. The script has been enabled\n\nI should inform the user that the configuration is complete."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 233719, "output_tokens": 2196, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 85622.36159999156}, "judge": null}
